# Cloudflare Pages response headers. Vite copies public/ into dist/, so this ships with
# the build. GitHub Pages could not do this at all — it is one of the two reasons the site
# moved to Pages (the other is _redirects).

# The tool pages load wasm-vips, which spawns pthreads and so wants SharedArrayBuffer,
# which requires cross-origin isolation. Scoped to the tool routes rather than sitewide:
# COEP also constrains cross-origin subresources, and the rest of the site pulls Google
# Fonts (src/index.css) and fetches privacy policies from raw.githubusercontent.com
# (AppPrivacy.jsx) — neither needs isolation.
#
# VERIFIED, and the one thing here that is easy to get wrong: the pattern must be
# /:lang/tools/* — a placeholder segment, NOT /*/tools/*. Cloudflare Pages only honours a
# splat at the END of a path, so a middle splat silently matches nothing at all. Observed
# on bibliofuse.pages.dev 2026-09-10: /*/tools/* returned no COOP/COEP whatsoever while
# /wasm/* (trailing splat) applied correctly.
/:lang/tools/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless

# The isolation headers and ACAO below mirror what lokaltools.com serves for the same
# wasm-vips build (byte-identical vips.js, md5 verified).
#
# Honest history, so nobody re-derives it: these were added while chasing a tool failure
# that turned out not to exist. The browser pane used for testing reported
# visibilityState:hidden, which throttles workers, and the probe re-loaded the emscripten
# factory while the component's own getVips() was already pending — which deadlocks. The
# ERR_BLOCKED_BY_RESPONSE entries that seemed to confirm a header problem were stale
# buffer from earlier deploys. The tools were working the whole time.
#
# So: this set is known-good and matches a known-good reference, but COOP and ACAO on the
# asset responses are NOT demonstrated to be load-bearing. Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy
# was tried here and removed; it is also not demonstrated to break anything. If you want
# to trim any of it, trim one line at a time and test a real conversion on the deployed
# site in a FRONTED, VISIBLE tab — the local dev server sets COEP on every response, so
# none of this reproduces before deploying.
/wasm/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *

/workers/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: credentialless
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
